[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-133764"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/assets/f6cbd594db6ab2454844d744ce1b776c3f561c4a6295abb9222ad2416c9f9292.png)\n\nDetermine the equation of the trend line shown above." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(2,8)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(8,5).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-8}{8-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{6} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=-\\frac{1}{2}$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can find this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(2,8):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{1}{2}x+b \\\\ 8 & =-\\frac{1}{2}(2)+b \\\\ 8 & =-1+b \\\\ 9 & =b \\\\ b & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x+9.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-134002/selection/7f0f0f045fee687959cefd1fb823e3741a6ca7aa10cf391f45fc270bca933a99" :answer/id #uuid "8664c7c9-bd00-50c7-a032-33818b2fff58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134002/selection/5ef0929f04483b2494dada1ca68b9bd1a0b323c0e584aa8883fbe86d6b02444c" :answer/id #uuid "3199f78e-71f5-5d52-a8bb-857194812e28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134002/selection/ec3dc34b21ac350807bcbba961b861de311aba9726d08b33967e6be5726343a1" :answer/id #uuid "08d27e2b-694e-5013-addc-4090aecfe1b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 